<%# The queue, a rail on the right that mirrors the library on the left. It is
    data-turbo-permanent so it and the order it holds survive navigation; the
    player controller fills it.

    Closed by default; `is-open` is what opens it, and the CSS decides what open
    means. On a desktop it stands beside the content. On a phone there is no
    beside — a 390px screen split in two shows neither half — so it comes over
    the top instead. It used to do neither: the button that opens it was hidden
    below md, and the class it toggled had no effect there anyway, so on a phone
    the queue simply did not exist. %>
<aside id="queue-panel" data-turbo-permanent data-player-target="panel"
       data-controller="panel" data-panel-name-value="queue" data-panel-edge-value="left"
       style="--panel: var(--queue)"
       class="panel rail shrink-0 flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-2xl surface">
  <%= render "shared/grip", side: "left-0" %>

  <div class="flex shrink-0 items-center justify-between gap-2 border-b border-white/10 py-3 pl-2 pr-4">
    <div class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1">
      <button type="button" data-action="player#toggleQueue" aria-label="Collapse queue"
              class="shrink-0 rounded-full p-1.5 text-neutral-400 transition hover:bg-white/10 hover:text-white">
        <svg class="size-4" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M5.72 3.22a.75.75 0 0 1 1.06 0l4.28 4.25a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.06l-4.28 4.25a.75.75 0 1 1-1.06-1.06L9.44 8 5.72 4.28a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.06Z"/>
        </svg>
      </button>
      <h2 class="truncate text-sm font-semibold text-white">Playing Next</h2>
    </div>
    <%# The queue loops when repeat is on, so it says so. %>
    <span data-player-target="repeatBadge" hidden
          class="flex shrink-0 items-center gap-1 rounded-full bg-accent/12 px-2 py-0.5 text-[11px] font-semibold text-accent ring-1 ring-inset ring-accent/25">
      <svg class="size-3" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M0 4.75A3.75 3.75 0 0 1 3.75 1h8.5A3.75 3.75 0 0 1 16 4.75v5a3.75 3.75 0 0 1-3.75 3.75H9.81l1.018 1.018a.75.75 0 1 1-1.06 1.06L6.939 12.75l2.829-2.828a.75.75 0 1 1 1.06 1.06L9.811 12h2.439a2.25 2.25 0 0 0 2.25-2.25v-5a2.25 2.25 0 0 0-2.25-2.25h-8.5A2.25 2.25 0 0 0 1.5 4.75v5A2.25 2.25 0 0 0 3.75 12H5v1.5H3.75A3.75 3.75 0 0 1 0 9.75v-5Z"/>
      </svg>
      <span data-player-target="repeatBadgeText">Repeat</span>
    </span>
  </div>
  <%# The queue and what the rail would offer after it scroll as one column: the
      offers stand where the queue ran out, which is the whole point of them. %>
  <div class="min-h-0 flex-1 overflow-y-auto p-2">
    <%# Drag a row to reorder what's coming; the × that surfaces on hover drops it. %>
    <ol data-player-target="queue" class="space-y-0.5"></ol>

    <%# What is left of the artist once the record ends. Dimmed on purpose: these
        are not queued, they are only on offer, and the rail should not read as
        though the music has ten more songs lined up when it has none. %>
    <ol data-player-target="suggestions" hidden class="space-y-0.5"></ol>
  </div>
  <p data-player-target="queueEmpty" class="shrink-0 px-4 pb-4 pt-1 text-sm text-neutral-500">Nothing up next.</p>

  <%# Which build this is, in the last corner of the app. The question "did the
      thing I just merged actually land?" should be answered by looking, not by
      going to the machine and asking Docker. %>
  <% if app_version.known? %>
    <p class="shrink-0 select-none px-4 pb-3 text-right text-[11px] text-neutral-600">Mediateca <%= app_version %></p>
  <% end %>
</aside>
